# A tunnel mode is required. This file accepts tunnel settings only, not secrets.
#
# Recommended: your own HTTPS origin. Run your reverse tunnel separately.
# Replace the example URL.
RADIO999K_TUNNEL=external
RADIO999K_PUBLIC_URL=https://radio.example.com

# Testing without a domain: comment out both lines above, then enable:
# RADIO999K_TUNNEL=tunnl
# The owner-private SSH files in --home have fixed names:
# pigeonmq-cloud-tunnel-ed25519 and pigeonmq-cloud-tunnel-known_hosts.

# Loopback testing only, even if process variables are set:
# 999k run --home "$CLOUD_HOME" --local-only

# Optional external connector example (run separately, not a 999K setting):
# cloudflared tunnel run --token-file /absolute/private/path/cloudflared.token
# Do not put Cloudflare tokens, 999K Bearer tokens, or other credentials here.
